the stunningly animated riot and the  last dragon  introduces disney's first southeast  asian princess  the fantasy world of kumandra and its  mystical water dragons  curiously hidden in the movie are many  references easter eggs and similarities  to disney's previous animated hit frozen  2.  yupikai movie lovers i'm jan and in this  video i'm revealing all the secret  connections details and parallels  between  raya sisu and disney's ice queen elsa  plus stick around to the end of the  video to find out about the original  much darker ending disney had planned  for the last dragon  spoilers ahead of course so take care  many disney fans have noticed an  interesting visual and somewhat uncanny  similarity between sisu and elsa  in particular sisu's face which has  extra large and expressive eyes  it's interesting because the final  version of sisu in the movie has some  notable differences from the original  concept art of the dragon which had much  smaller eyes and sharper teeth and fangs  sisu is also predominantly blue in the  final movie with only touches of purple  whereas she had a lot more purple in the  initial design  as well as some white colors this  dominant blue coloring on sisu makes the  magical dragon more reminiscent of elsa  whose signature colour has often been  blue as well  and many fans are so convinced about the  visual similarities of the two  that they jokingly suggest elsa got  bored of being the fifth spirit after a  few years and decided to become a dragon  of course both sisu and elsa's abilities  are water-based so naturally the colour  blue fits them both well  too and i'll be talking more about the  water dragons in the film  shortly it's interesting how key moments  in both rya and the last dragon and  frozen two  occur when the main protagonists  encounter the remains of a shipwreck  raya comes across the wreckage of a boat  after her search for the river's end  where legend says that sisu is sleeping  inside the ship as raya summons sisu the  water  in the stream reverses direction large  drops float into the air and combine to  reform as the legendary water dragon  this feels reminiscent of frozen two  where elsa used her magic to pull water  that was embedded in the hull of the  wrecked ship to create an  ice sculpture that held the memories of  the last moments of her parents  and raya's comment when she sees a ship  for the first time  six years of searching and we end up at  a literal  shipwreck feels like a wink to frozen  fans about their six-year wait between  the first and second movie for the  reveal of the truth about what had  really happened to elsewhere and anna's  parents king agnar and queen oduna  in riot and the last dragon we learned  that 500 years ago the world  came under attack from the droon  amorphous and destructive spirits who  turned both people and dragons into  stone  four of the only five surviving dragons  decided to combine their powers and  magic  into a dragon gem which they entrusted  to their sibling sisu the fifth dragon  who then used the power of the gem to  defeat the plague of droon  similarly in frozen two it's the fifth  spirit elsa who together with honor  breaks the curse on the enchanted forest  and saves arendelle from destruction  in both movies there are five magical  elements  in raya each of the five dragons has a  distinct power  this is my little sister ambas magic i  got the glow  and that's prani she's a shape-shifter  fog that was my brother jagan's magic  and pangu he's our big brother he brings  the reign  i'm a really strong swimmer  and in frozen two there are five spirits  gale the wind element bruni the fire  spirit the earth giants the knock water  spirit  and elsa the fifth spirit who together  with her sister honor forms a bridge  connecting nature with humanity  the importance of five elements in riot  and the last dragon is also emphasized  in the very opening shot of the movie  with this picture of a stone structure  with five curved supports holding up the  top  one of these is broken signaling either  how the world is broken or perhaps  pointing to the missing fifth dragon  sisu who raya is searching for  there's also five stone balls with the  four smaller ones on the outside  representing the four dragons who gave  their powers to create the dragon gem  which is represented by the large ball  in the center  and there are of course five kingdoms in  kumandra and at the end of the story one  person from each of the five kingdoms  come together to save their world  now in many traditions numbers also have  a symbolic  quality with the number five often  symbolizing  balance mankind health and love even  bearing this in mind though it's still  intriguing that disney has chosen to  feature this particular symbolism in  both of their most recent animated  features  in both movies too our protagonists end  up sacrificing themselves or temporarily  dying as they  reach the end of their quest for raya  she's the first in her group to give her  piece of the dragon gem to namari and  trust in her  assisi wanted her to without the gem's  protection the droon turn  rya to stone similar to how elsa froze  entirely when she dove too deep into  atta harlan's memories  and in the first frozen movie anna too  turned to ice when she sacrificed  herself to save elsa from the evil huns  nobody stays dead and rya comes back to  life after  namari puts the dragon gem back together  which unleashes the power of the dragons  on the drone  while in frozen two elsa is unfrozen  when anna lifts the curse on the  enchanted forest by destroying the  arendellian dam  another interesting similarity between  both films is the importance of water to  the final resolution  in roya and the last dragon the rain  which falls liberates everyone from  their stony fate  whereas in frozen two when the dam  breaks the resulting tsunami almost  destroys arendelle as it flows down the  fjord towards the kingdom  until elsa arrives in the nick of time  to stop it  water is of course a hugely important  motif in raya and the last dragon  as it's the only element other than the  dragon gem itself which can ward off the  drone  they're repelled by water and tellingly  raya is even called dewdrop by her  father benja  sisu is also a water dragon and her  design as well as her siblings was  inspired by the southeast asian naga  mythical divine or semi-divine beings  the naga are often more serpentine in  appearance than the european style of  dragon usually depicted in disney movies  and they're sometimes associated with  the mekong river which was actually the  inspiration for the dragon-shaped river  that runs through and connects all of  kumandra's five kingdoms  this is water it's sort of my thing but  sisu also has a curious parallel with  frozen two's elemental water spirit the  noc  though that is of course based on  scandinavian mythology  in the original folklore the knock has  the ability to shapeshift and turn into  a man or woman much like sisu does in  riot and the last dragon  i just shape changed into people dragons  can do that  look at my my people arms and my people  face look how close my butt is to my  head  while the nagger that sisu is based on  are also sometimes portrayed as half  human half serpent  and as always the frozen fandom has been  quick to catch on to these similarities  swapping out an image of the knock for  sisu in this picture of elsa after she  stops the flood  another thematic similarity between raya  and the last dragon and frozen 2  is how human discord and treachery  triggers a kind of natural or mystical  antagonist which is something  disney has explored in other recent  films like moana in contrast to more  conventional animated villains such as  maleficent and cruella deville  when the maori portrays ryan's trust to  try and steal the dragon gem for the  fang people it causes all of kumandra's  kingdoms to fight each other over the  stone and when they end up breaking the  gem it awakens the droon who now pose an  existential threat to all of kumandra  likewise in frozen 2  it was king runard's betrayal of an  attack on the north uldra which angered  the spirits who then cursed the  enchanted forest  trapping everyone inside and preventing  anyone from entering or leaving  an especially interesting detail about  both movies is that at one time disney  originally had much darker endings  planned for both of them  in raya and the last dragon sisu dies  when namari betrays raya again and the  subsequent confrontation goes wrong  in an interview with polygon the  filmmakers explained that sisu  dying was always part of the original  plan so that raya would learn the dragon  wasn't somebody who would magically  rescue commander from the drone and that  instead she and the others would have to  learn to trust one another in order to  defeat them  just like sisu and the other dragons had  done 500 years before  in the final film sisu is resurrected  later on together with all her dragon  siblings  however there was a version of the movie  where sisi remained dead after the rain  fell  and no other dragons were resurrected  either meaning sisu was  literally the last dragon as one of the  film's producers pointed out if humans  are the solution  why are we bringing the magical mystical  creatures back  in the end though the filmmakers felt  they wanted to go with a happy  ending and a big disney moment that  makes your heart sing  and so sisu and the dragons came back  now  depending on your viewpoint the original  ending might have been more striking  because it would have solidified the  sacrifice the dragons made for kumandra  and made the consequences of human  discord and strife more long-lasting  likewise frozen too almost had a much  darker ending where arendelle castle was  destroyed by the flood from the broken  dam  making the consequences of king runard's  betrayal of the northuldra more  impactful  the original scene of the aftermath also  shows how honour planned to use the  destruction as an opportunity for  renewal in the kingdom  we'll rebuild the castle new no secrets  no deceit new rules even and if you want  to learn more about frozen two's other  deleted scenes there's a card here and a  link in the video description  another notable detail is the diamond  pattern on the walls of the heartland  palace  which reminds me of the diamonds that  suddenly appeared over arendelle during  into the unknown  this could be a frozen two easter egg or  it could likely be a reference to the  diamond motifs you can see on  fang jewellery such as those on chief  verana's earring and neck ring  given we see these diamond patterns just  as raya is confiding in namari and is  about to take her to see the dragon gem  it might be a clue to the imminent fang  betrayal  so did you spot any other interesting  easter eggs or details in the movie  comment with your thoughts and theories  below and if you enjoyed this don't  forget to leave a thumbs up it's really  appreciated  you can also tap left for those frozen  two deleted scenes and alternate ending  or tap right for something else you're  sure to like  thanks for watching and see you next  time yupikai movie lovers
 

